{
  "moduleId": "m00334",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00334:title:auto-1",
    "text": "Catabolism of Carbohydrates: Glycolysis"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "ea0d308f-afd6-49fc-95ee-89bd01e6a071"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00334:caption:fig-00001-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "The catabolism of alpha-glucose to glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate via five steps. Adenosine triphosphate converts to adenosine diphosphate in this process."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00334:caption:fig-00002-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "The remaining five steps of glucose catabolism. Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate converts to 1,3-bisphosphoglycerate. 3-phosphoglycerate, 2-phosphoglycerate, phosphoenolpyruvate and pyruvate are formed in seventh, eighth, ninth and tenth steps, repectively."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00001",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00334:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "Steps 1–2 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Phosphorylation and Isomerization"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00002",
          "class": null,
          "title": null,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00002",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00002"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00003",
              "class": "scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00334:caption:fig-00003-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00003-alt",
                  "text": "The isomerization of glucose-6-phosphate. Alpha-glucose-6-phosphate undergoes a reversible reaction to form an enediol that leads to an intermediate followed by the final product alpha-fructose-6-phosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_003.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00003",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00334:title:sect-00003-title",
            "text": "Step 3 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Phosphorylation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00003",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00003"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00004",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00004-alt",
                  "text": "Alpha-fructose-6-phosphate isomerizes to beta-fructose-6-phosphate.  Condensation with adenosine triphosphate provides  beta-fructose 1,6-bisphosphate and adenosine diphosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_004.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00004",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00334:title:sect-00004-title",
            "text": "Step 4 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Cleavage"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00004",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00004"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00005",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00005-alt",
                  "text": "Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate reacts reversibly to form glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate and another intermediate compound. The intermediate further reacts with base and forms dihydroxyacetone phosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_005.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00005",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00005"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00006",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00006"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00006",
              "class": "scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00334:caption:fig-00006-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00006-alt",
                  "text": "Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate forms an iminium ion that leads to glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate and an enamine, the enamine isomerizes to an iminium ion , which is protonated  by H-A to form dihydroxyacetone phosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_006.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00005",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00334:title:sect-00005-title",
            "text": "Step 5 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Isomerization"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00007",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00007"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00007",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00007-alt",
                  "text": "Dihydroxyacetone phosphate is protonated to form cis enediol which isomerizes to glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate. The carbon in dihydroxyacetone phosphate is numbered from bottom to top."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_007.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00006",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00334:title:sect-00006-title",
            "text": "Steps 6–7 of [[xref:fig-00002]]: Oxidation, Phosphorylation, and Dephosphorylation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00008",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00008"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00008",
              "class": "scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00334:caption:fig-00008-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00008-alt",
                  "text": "Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate is converted to 1,3-bisphosphoglycerate via a nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate cation-mediated oxidation of a hemithioacetal intermediate,  which undergoes a thioester condensation, and elimination to provide  1,3-bisphosphoglycerate. "
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_008.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00009",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00009"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00009",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00009-alt",
                  "text": "1,3-Bisphosphoglycerate is mono-dephosphorylated via the condensation with magnesium adenosine diphosphate to form a phosphorated ester intermediate that undergoes elimination of adenosine triphosphate and 3-phosphoglycerate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_009.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00007",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00334:title:sect-00007-title",
            "text": "Step 8 of [[xref:fig-00002]]: Isomerization"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00010",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00010"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00010",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00010-alt",
                  "text": "3-Phosphoglycerate is phosphorylated by a phosphoglycerate mutase to provide a 2,3-bisphosphoglycerate intermediate, which  is enzymatically dephosphorylated to  2-phosphoglycerate, and the rephosphorylated mutase. "
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_010.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00008",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00334:title:sect-00008-title",
            "text": "Steps 9–10 of [[xref:fig-00002]]: Dehydration and Dephosphorylation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00011",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00011"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00011",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00011-alt",
                  "text": "The magnesium salt of 2-phosphoglycerate  reacts with a base to form a phosphoglycerate anion which is dehydrated to provide phosphoenol pyruvate and water."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_011.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00012",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00012"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00012",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00012-alt",
                  "text": "Phosphoenol pyruvate reacts with the magnesium salt of adenosine diphosphate and water to form an enol pyruvate which isomerizes  to  pyruvate and  adenosine triphosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_012.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00013",
              "segmentId": "m00334:para:para-00013"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00013",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00334:alt:fig-00013-alt",
                  "text": "Glucose reacts with two moles  each of nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide cation, phosphate and adenosine diphosphate to form two moles of pyruvate, nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate hydride, adenosine triphosphate, and water."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_05_013.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
